section: compiler
synopsis: Speed up type-family-heavy programs by zapping coercions
issues: #8095 #27336 #27518
mrs: !16378
description: {
  GHC now erases the coercions that it produces when reducing type family
  applications, keeping only their endpoints and the assumptions they used
  (a process called "zapping").
  This greatly speeds up the compilation of type-family-heavy programs (#8095).

  This behaviour is controlled by ``-fzap-coercions`` and enabled by default;
  disable with ``-fno-zap-coercions``.
}
